## 3. Off-Slot Prompt Cache Lookup

`server_prompt_cache::load()` in `server-task.cpp:1737` searches the cache for a better match than the slot's current prompt:

```cpp
// server-task.cpp:1737
bool server_prompt_cache::load(server_prompt & prompt, const server_tokens & tokens_new,
                                llama_context * ctx_tgt, llama_context * ctx_dft, int32_t id_slot) {
    const int lcp_best = prompt.tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

    float f_keep_best = prompt.tokens.size() > 0 ? float(lcp_best) / prompt.tokens.size() : -1.0f;
    float sim_best    = float(lcp_best) / tokens_new.size();

    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
        const int lcp_cur = it->prompt.tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

        const float f_keep_cur = float(lcp_cur) / it->prompt.tokens.size();
        const float sim_cur    = float(lcp_cur) / tokens_new.size();

        // don't trash large prompts
        if (f_keep_cur < 0.25f) {
            continue;
        }

        if (f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && sim_best < sim_cur) {
            f_keep_best = f_keep_cur;
            sim_best    = sim_cur;
            it_best = it;
        }
    }

    if (it_best != states.end()) {
        // restore KV state from cache entry into the slot
        llama_state_seq_set_data_ext(ctx_tgt, it_best->data.main.data(), size, id_slot, 0);
        prompt = std::move(it_best->prompt);
        states.erase(it_best);
    }
    return true;
}
```

The cache uses a dual metric:
- **`f_keep`** — what fraction of the *cached* prompt is preserved (avoids trashing large cached prompts)
- **`sim`** — what fraction of the *new* prompt is covered by cache (prefers better coverage)

A `f_keep < 0.25f` threshold prevents evicting large cache entries for marginal gains.

