## How Prompt Cache / Slot Reuse Works

There are **two layers** of caching:

### Layer 1: Slot-Level LCP Matching (in-KV-cache reuse)

When a new request arrives, `get_available_slot()` (`server-context.cpp:1530`) tries to find a slot whose **existing KV cache** shares a long common prefix with the new prompt. This avoids re-decoding already-computed tokens.

```cpp
// server-context.cpp:1530-1600 (excerpt)
server_slot * get_available_slot(const server_task & task) {
    server_slot * ret = nullptr;
    bool update_cache = false;

    // 1) Explicit slot ID requested
    if (task.id_slot != -1) {
        ret = get_slot_by_id(task.id_slot);
        if (ret) {
            SLT_INF(*ret, "selected slot by id (%d)\n", task.id_slot);
        }
    }

    // 2) LCP similarity search — find slot with longest common prefix
    if (slot_prompt_similarity != 0.0f) {
        float sim_best = 0;
        for (server_slot & slot : slots) {
            if (task.id_slot != -1 && slot.id != task.id_slot) continue;
            if (slot.is_processing()) continue;
            if (slot.prompt.tokens.empty()) continue;

            // fraction of LCP length / input prompt length
            const float sim_cur = float(tokens.get_common_prefix(task.tokens)) / task.tokens.size();

            if (sim_cur > sim_best && sim_cur > slot_prompt_similarity) {
                sim_best = sim_cur;
                ret = &slot;
            }
        }

        if (ret != nullptr) {
            const float f_keep = (sim_best*task.tokens.size()) / ret->prompt.tokens.size();
            SLT_INF(*ret, "selected slot by LCP similarity, sim_best = %.3f (> %.3f thold), f_keep = %.3f\n",
                    sim_best, slot_prompt_similarity, f_keep);

            // if we'd lose >50% of existing context, save it to the off-chip cache first
            if (f_keep < 0.5f) {
                update_cache = true;
            }
        }
    }

    // 3) LRU fallback — pick least-recently-used idle slot
    if (ret == nullptr) {
        int64_t t_last = -1;
        for (server_slot & slot : slots) {
            if (slot.is_processing()) continue;
            if (!ret || slot.t_last_used <= t_last) {
                t_last = slot.t_last_used;
                ret = &slot;
            }
        }
        if (ret != nullptr) {
            SLT_TRC(*ret, "selected slot by LRU, t_last = %" PRId64 "\n", t_last);
            update_cache = true;
        }
    }

    // 4) If reusing a slot with different content, save old prompt to off-chip cache
    if (ret) {
        update_cache = update_cache && prompt_cache;
        update_cache = update_cache && task.type == SERVER_TASK_TYPE_COMPLETION;
        if (update_cache) {
            ret->prompt_save(*prompt_cache);           // save old KV state to disk/ram cache
            if (!ret->prompt_load(*prompt_cache, task.tokens)) {
                ret->prompt_clear();                    // fallback: clear if no cache match found
            }
            prompt_cache->update();                     // evict oldest entries if over limit
        }
    }
    return ret;
}
```

### Layer 2: Off-Chip Prompt Cache (`server_prompt_cache`)

When a slot is reassigned and its old KV cache would be lost, the current state is saved to an off-chip cache (RAM-backed, bounded by `--cache-ram-mib`). Later, when loading a new prompt into that slot, `server_prompt_cache::load()` searches for a cached entry with the best LCP match:

